 Bank Credit & Debit Analysis — Power BI
Overview
This module contains the Power BI dashboard for analyzing banking credit and debit transactions.

The dashboard converts transaction-level data into interactive KPIs, charts, trends, and business insights.

Objectives
Build an interactive banking dashboard.
Monitor credit and debit performance.
Analyze customer transaction behavior.
Analyze branch and account performance.
Identify transaction trends.
Provide business-focused insights.
Dashboard Pages
Page 1 — Executive Overview
KPIs:

Total Transactions
Total Credit
Total Debit
Total Customers
Average Transaction Amount
Visuals:

Credit vs Debit
Monthly Transaction Trend
Transaction Category
Customer Segment
Branch Performance
Page 2 — Credit Analysis
Total Credit
Credit Transaction Count
Monthly Credit Trend
Credit by Category
Credit by Customer
Credit by Branch
Page 3 — Debit Analysis
Total Debit
Debit Transaction Count
Monthly Debit Trend
Debit by Category
Debit by Customer
Debit by Branch
Page 4 — Customer Analysis
Top 10 Customers
Customer Transaction Value
Customer Transaction Count
Customer Segment Analysis
Average Transaction per Customer
Recommended Data Model
             Date
              │
              │
Customer ── Transactions ── Account
              │
              ├── Branch
              │
              └── Category
Example DAX Measures
Total Transactions
Total Transactions =
COUNTROWS(BankTransactions)
Total Credit
Total Credit =
CALCULATE(
    SUM(BankTransactions[Amount]),
    BankTransactions[Transaction_Type] = "Credit"
)
Total Debit
Total Debit =
CALCULATE(
    SUM(BankTransactions[Amount]),
    BankTransactions[Transaction_Type] = "Debit"
)
Average Transaction
Average Transaction =
AVERAGE(BankTransactions[Amount])
Net Transaction Value
Net Transaction Value =
[Total Credit] - [Total Debit]
Filters
Dashboard users can filter by:

Date
Transaction Type
Transaction Category
Customer
Customer Segment
Account Type
Branch
City
Payment Mode
